      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chevy_Chase_View%2C_Maryland",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Real‑estate developer Claude Livingstone designed the town a year earlier and then sold the plan to Harry E. Smith.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chevy_Chase_View%2C_Maryland",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s streets follow an irregular grid that has stayed largely unchanged since the original layout.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.chevychaseviewmd.gov/1198/History",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Connecticut Avenue bisects Chevy Chase View, while the Capital Beltway circles the area just a mile to the south.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chevy_Chase_View%2C_Maryland",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Chevy Chase Historical Society curates exhibitions that showcase the most interesting people, places and events in the town’s history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
